    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0731" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Brazil/5388: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-02T17:00:00-03:00">December 2, 1943—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5560. President Vargas has approved rice agreement quoted in my 5474, November
                    25, 5 p.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d673-f1"/> and London has approved with minor
                    modifications. Awaiting suggestions interested agencies in Washington.<anchor
                        n="25" xml:id="d673-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d673-f1" n="24" xml:id="d673-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the agreement provided for the purchase by the United States and the
                    United Kingdom of the exportable surplus of rice in accordance with a specified
                    schedule. It recognized a system of rice quotas which Brazil might ship to the
                    other American Republics. Brazil agreed to prevent the imposition of additional
                    taxes and to give publicity to the agreement. (811.20 Defense (M)
                    Brazil/5376)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d673-f2" n="25" xml:id="d673-f2-content">
                <p>The agreement was acceptable to United States agencies with some modifications
                    concerning inspection, storage, and insurance. Notes embodying the agreement
                    (not printed) were signed and exchanged on December 21, 1943. (811.20 Defense
                    (M) Brazil/5421)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
